  "title": "TLS: Get rid of an unaligned hash",
  "description": "This is not a particularly hot path (except in the cases where someone\nhas a truly enormous SSLKEYLOGFILE, and even then it's pretty small\ncompared to the text processing, see #17051), so it's not worth\ncasting uint8_t array (that in practical cases, is a length divisible\nby 8 or at least 4) to an unsigned in order to do a relatively fast\nXOR \"hash\" (because the things being hashed, mostly a CLIENT_RANDOM\nare already supposed to be cryptographically random a secure hash is\nnot that necessary), because that leads to UB from unaligned access\nexcept when the StringInfo has its memory very carefully allocated,\nwhich it doesn't currently in all cases.\n\nClang compiled with UBSAN will in some cases complain about runtime\nunaligned access:\n\n/home/johnthacker/git/wireshark/epan/dissectors/packet-tls-utils.c:6380:24: runtime error: load of misaligned address 0x7b4c9f061053 for type 'const unsigned int', which requires 4 byte alignment\n0x7b4c9f061053: note: pointer points here\n 00  00 00 00 46 3a 96 b2 4e  47 fb f7 35 20 fb 40 97  df fd e4 34 13 d8 a8 23  19 d3 f0 67 a7 d6 35\n              ^\nSUMMARY: UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer: undefined-behavior /home/johnthacker/git/wireshark/epan/dissectors/packet-tls-utils.c:6380:24\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
